<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Using logarithms to determine the age of an archeological sample</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Carbon-14 has a half-life of 5730 years. The percentage \(P\) of the original carbon-14 left in a sample after \(t\) years is</p>
\[ P = 100\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{t/5730}. \]
<p><strong>(a)</strong> A piece of charcoal from an ancient cooking fire has \({@P1d@}\%\) of its carbon-14 left. How old is it?</p>
<p>\(t =\) [[input:ans1]] years [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> A bone tool from an archaeological site has \({@P2@}\%\) of its carbon-14 left. Use logarithms to find its age, to the nearest 10 years.</p>
<p>\(t =\) [[input:ans2]] years [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \(\dfrac{{@P1d@}}{100} = \dfrac{1}{{@2^j@}} = \left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)^{@j@}\). So \(\dfrac{t}{5730} = {@j@}\), and \(t = {@j@} \times 5730 = {@ta1@}\) years: \({@j@}\) half-lives.</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Divide by 100, then take logarithms of both sides and use the power law:</p>
\[ \frac{{@P2@}}{100} = \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{t/5730} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad \log {@float(P2/100)@} = \frac{t}{5730}\log\frac{1}{2} \]
\[ t = 5730 \times \frac{\log {@float(P2/100)@}}{\log 0.5} = {@float(ex2)@}\ldots \approx {@ta2@} \text{ years}. \]
<p>The graph shows how the percentage left falls by half every 5730 years, with both samples marked.</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of the percentage of carbon-14 left against age in years, halving every 5730 years. The charcoal is marked at ({#ta1#}, {#P1d#}) and the bone tool at ({#ta2#}, {#P2#}).">
[[jsxgraph width="380px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var X0 = 0, X1 = {#max(ta1, ta2)*1.15/1000#}, Y1 = 105, P = [[{#ta1/1000#}, {#float(P1)#}, 'charcoal'], [{#float(ex2)/1000#}, {#P2#}, 'bone tool']];
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[X0 - (X1 - X0)*0.12, Y1*1.08, X1, -Y1*0.12], axis:true, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false, pan:{enabled:false}, zoom:{enabled:false}});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x){ return 100*Math.pow(0.5, x/5.73); }, X0, X1], {strokeColor:'#1f5fa8', strokeWidth:2, highlight:false});

  for (var i = 0; i < P.length; i++) { var right = P[i][0] > X0 + 0.6*(X1 - X0);   // labels on the right half go to the left of the point
    b.create('point', [P[i][0], P[i][1]], {name:P[i][2], size:3, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b', showInfobox:false,
      label:{offset:[right ? -8 : 8, 10], anchorX:right ? 'right' : 'left', fontSize:12, cssStyle:'background:rgba(255,255,255,0.85)'}}); }
  b.create('text', [X1, -Y1*0.07, 't (thousand years)'], {anchorX:'right', fontSize:13, fixed:true});
  b.create('text', [X0 - (X1 - X0)*0.1, Y1*1.03, 'P (%)'], {fontSize:13, fixed:true});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
